From d48e62a277ca0cc15cccaff1e8d3c8e9de5e0f28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AEON-7 <aeon-7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:14:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [AEON M2] inkling2 gfx12: K/V tap projections in the qkvr
 GEMV launch; one message mix per loop pass

- ops/gemv.py: gemv3x runs the K/V dynamic tap projections in extra
  programs of the qkvr GEMV (bitwise equal to separate GEMVs); main row
  blocks keep unmasked loads. Used for M <= 4 (AEON_FUSE_TAPS,
  AEON_FUSE_TAPS_MAX_M); at M=8 it measured slower in bs8 decode.
- loop.py: the message bank is fixed per pass, so all core layer messages
  are one attn-res launch per pass (AEON_BATCH_MESSAGES), read from the
  stack without a bank copy. Bit-exact.

gen_bench (R9700 GPU0, graph): bs1 79.2, bs8 373.1 tok/s. KL (max-batched 8,
60 prompts) 0.00219, top-1 98.12%. Chats: 0 loops.
Hook point unchanged: HOOKS.oproj right after o_proj in attention.forward.
Original AEON work (clean room), Apache-2.0.
